Impact of Climate Damage on Reliable Water Supply=
	Climate Damage Fraction OLD
	~	Dmnl
	~	A parameter that determines the impact of climate risk on water resources \
		or infrastructure availability to provide reliable water supply.
	|

MIN Industrial Water Use[Regions]=
	2e+07,
	2e+08,
	2e+10,
	2e+08,
	2e+10
	~	m*m*m/Year [2e+09,2e+10]
	~	Min level of average industrial water use.
	|

Reliable Water Supply= INTEG (
	Net Change in Reliable Water Supply,
		INIT Reliable Water Supply)
	~	m*m*m/Year
	~	Amount of water that can be reliably provided on annual basis for \
		domestic, agricultural and industrial use due to resources and \
		infrastructure availability. Source of historical data: 2030 Water \
		Resources Group, 2009. Charting Our Water Future - Economic frameworks to \
		inform decision-making. \
		http://www.mckinsey.com/App_Media/Reports/Water/Charting_Our_Water_Future_F\
		ull_Report_001.pdf
	|

Reference Temperature=
	3
	~	DegreesC
	~	Reference Temperature for Calculation of Climate Damages.
	|

Available Water Resources= INTEG (
	Recovery of Used Water Resources Rate+Water Supply Rate-Agricultural Water Withdrawal Rate\
		-Domestic Water Withdrawal Rate-Industrial Water Withdrawal Rate-Drought Out,
		Desired Available Water Resources)
	~	m*m*m
	~	Available water resources to be used for domestic, agricultural and \
		industrial use.
	|

Available Water Resources Adjustment=
	(Desired Available Water Resources-Available Water Resources)/Available Water Resources Adjustment Time
	~	m*m*m/Year
	~	Adjustment of available water resources to desired available water \
		resources.
	|

Available Water Resources Adjustment Time=
	1
	~	Year
	~	Time required to adjust available water resources to desired water \
		resources.
	|

Water Supply Fulfillment Rate=
	2/(1+EXP(-Water Supply Fulfillment Factor*(Reliable Water Supply/Desired Water Supply Rate\
		)))-1
	~	Dmnl
	~	Nonlinear relation that describes water supply fulfillment as a relation \
		of water supply and demand. With growing water demand the supply \
		fulfillment might be impaired which relates to infrastructure design and \
		its operating limits.
	|

Water Quality Steepness=
	5
	~	Dmnl
	~	Steepness of nonlinear relation describing domestic water quality.
	|

Water Safety Stock Coverage=
	0.1
	~	Year
	~	Water resources safety stock expressed in terms of time duration. \
		Additional time period during which the water resources need to be \
		available at the total water demand level.
	|

Water Supply Fulfillment Factor=
	3
	~	Dmnl
	~	A factor determining the strength of infrastructure operating limits on \
		water supply fulfillment.
	|

Burke Damage long term pooled=
	Burke Damage long term pooled Lookup(Temperature Change from Preindustrial/unit DegreesC\
		)
	~	percent
	~		|

Net Climate Change Impact on Economy=
	1 - Climate Damage Percentage/"100 percent"
	~	Dmnl
	~	The fraction of ecomomy output after loss due to climate change.
	|

MIN Agricultural Water Use Irrigated[Regions]=
	0.00223878,
	0.01,
	0.002,
	0.002,
	0.002
	~	m*m*m/(Year*m*m) [0.002,0.01]
	~	Min level of average agricultural water use on part of agricultural land \
		that is irrigated.
	|

Min Reliable Water Supply Decrease Time=
	1
	~	Year
	~	Minimal period of time used to consider changes in water resources or \
		infrastructure availability.
	|

Max Water Withdrawal Rate=
	Available Water Resources/Min Water Withdrawal Time
	~	m*m*m/Year
	~	Max possible water withdrawal rate due to available water resources.
	|

Reference GWP per Capita for Agricultural Water Use Irrigated[Regions]=
	2000,
