CO2 Intensity of Fuels[Oil]=
	160*(0.000453592/0.025)*1e+06
	~	tCO2/Mtoe
	~	Coal: 220 (Pounds of CO2 emitted per million British thermal units for coal) * \
		0.000453592 (pound to ton) / 0.025 (milltion British thermal units to toe) \
		* 1e+6 (toe to Mtoe)
		Gas: 117 (Pounds of CO2 emitted per million British thermal units for coal) * \
		0.000453592 (pound to ton) / 0.025 (milltion British thermal units to toe) \
		* 1e+6 (toe to Mtoe)
		Oil: 160 (Pounds of CO2 emitted per million British thermal units for coal) * \
		0.000453592 (pound to ton) / 0.025 (milltion British thermal units to toe) \
		* 1e+6 (toe to Mtoe)
		
		Data from EIA: https://www.eia.gov/tools/faqs/faq.php?id=73&t=11
	|

INIT RODU[Regions]=
	0
	~	Dmnl
	~	Initial Ratio of Oil Fraction Discoverable to Undiscoverable.
		In the global version of FeliX: GET XLS \
		CONSTANTS('InitialValues.xlsx','Stocks','F13')
	|

Table for FIODT(
	[(0,0)-(1,1)],(0,0.8),(0.2,0.8),(0.4,0.7),(0.6,0.5),(0.8,0.2),(1,0))
	~	Dmnl
	~	Table determining order by which technology investments are dedicated to \
		exploration and production technologies. For small Oil Fraction \
		Discoverable, in order to make sufficient resources available to be \
		produced, more investments are directed to exploration technologies. Once \
		the Oil Fraction Discoverable increases the investments are redirected to \
		production technologies.
	|

