Average duration of tertiary education[Regions]=
	Lookup tertiary education duration[Regions](Time)
	~	Year
	~	In current International Standard Classification of Education (ISCED), \
		this is considered 5 years, but assumed to have changed over time, \
		starting from 2 years at the beginning of the century.
	|

Mean Years of Schooling[Regions]=
	(Average duration of primary education[Regions]*sum(Primary Education Graduates[Regions\
		,Gender!,MYS!])
	+(Average duration of secondary education[Regions]+Average duration of primary education\
		[Regions])*sum(Secondary Education Graduates[Regions,Gender!,MYS!])
	+(Average duration of tertiary education[Regions]+Average duration of secondary education\
		[Regions]+Average duration of primary education[Regions])*sum(Tertiary Education Graduates\
		[Regions,Gender!,MYS!]))/sum(Population Cohorts[Regions,Gender!,MYS!])
	~	Year
	~		|

Average duration of primary education[Regions]=
	SMOOTH(Lookup primary education duration[Regions](Time),1)
	~	Year
	~	In current International Standard Classification of Education (ISCED), \
		this is considered 6 years, but assumed to have changed over time, \
		starting from 2 years at the beginning of the century. Smoothed to avoid \
		sharpe changes.
	|

Average duration of secondary education[Regions]=
	SMOOTH(Lookup secondary education duration[Regions](Time),1)
	~	Year
	~	In current International Standard Classification of Education (ISCED), \
		this is considered 6 years, but assumed to have changed over time, \
		starting from 2 years at the beginning of the century. Smoothed to avoid \
		sharpe changes. More information is needed!!!
	|

